 r←ComposeDependencySetting(folder target)
⍝ The opposite of `ParseDependencySetting`: returns the value of a "tatin" or "nuget" dependency setting
⍝ for `folder` and `target`: '<folder>' when `target` is empty, otherwise '<folder>=<target>'.
⍝ Together with `ParseDependencySetting` this is the only function that knows how such a setting is written.
⍝ The result is not checked: pass it to `ParseDependencySetting` for that.
 r←folder,(0<≢target)/'=',target
⍝Done
